<file path="nginx/ssl/README.md">
# SSL Certificates Directory

This directory is mounted to `/etc/nginx/ssl` inside the `lumicorepro-nginx` container.

## Production Setup (Let's Encrypt / Certbot)
To enable HTTPS in production:

1. Obtain SSL certificates using Certbot:
   ```bash
   certbot certonly --standalone -d yourdomain.com -d api.yourdomain.com
   ```

2. Copy or link your certificates into this folder:
   - `fullchain.pem` -> `/etc/nginx/ssl/fullchain.pem`
   - `privkey.pem`   -> `/etc/nginx/ssl/privkey.pem`

3. In `nginx.conf`, uncomment the HTTPS server block:
   ```nginx
   server {
       listen 443 ssl http2;
       server_name yourdomain.com;

       ssl_certificate /etc/nginx/ssl/fullchain.pem;
       ssl_certificate_key /etc/nginx/ssl/privkey.pem;
       ssl_protocols TLSv1.2 TLSv1.3;
       ssl_ciphers HIGH:!aNULL:!MD5;
       ...
   }
   ```

## Development / Self-Signed Certificate
For local HTTPS testing, generate a self-signed certificate:
```bash
openssl req -x509 -nodes -days 365 -newkey rsa:2048 \
  -keyout nginx/ssl/server.key \
  -out nginx/ssl/server.crt \
  -subj "/C=US/ST=State/L=City/O=LumiCorePro/OU=Dev/CN=localhost"
```
</file>

<file path="nginx/nginx.conf">
worker_processes auto;

events {
  worker_connections 1024;
}

http {
  include       /etc/nginx/mime.types;
  default_type  application/octet-stream;

  log_format main '$remote_addr - $remote_user [$time_local] "$request" '
                  '$status $body_bytes_sent "$http_referer" '
                  '"$http_user_agent" "$http_x_forwarded_for"';

  access_log /var/log/nginx/access.log main;
  error_log  /var/log/nginx/error.log warn;
  sendfile   on;
  keepalive_timeout 65;
  gzip on;
  gzip_types text/css application/javascript application/json image/svg+xml;
  gzip_min_length 1000;

  # Rate limiting zones
  limit_req_zone $binary_remote_addr zone=api:10m rate=30r/s;
  limit_req_zone $binary_remote_addr zone=auth:10m rate=5r/s;

  upstream backend {
    server backend:5000;
  }

  upstream frontend {
    server frontend:5173;
  }

  server {
    listen       80;
    server_name  _;

    # Security headers
    add_header X-Frame-Options "SAMEORIGIN" always;
    add_header X-Content-Type-Options "nosniff" always;
    add_header X-XSS-Protection "1; mode=block" always;
    add_header Referrer-Policy "strict-origin-when-cross-origin" always;
    add_header Content-Security-Policy "default-src 'self' http: https: data: blob: 'unsafe-inline' 'unsafe-eval' ws: wss:;" always;

    # Backend API
    location /api/ {
      limit_req zone=api burst=50 nodelay;
      proxy_pass         http://backend;
      proxy_set_header   Host $host;
      proxy_set_header   X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
      proxy_set_header   X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
      proxy_set_header   X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
      proxy_http_version 1.1;
      proxy_set_header   Upgrade $http_upgrade;
      proxy_set_header   Connection "upgrade";
    }

    # Backend API (Auth endpoints with stricter rate limiting)
    location /api/auth {
      limit_req zone=auth burst=10 nodelay;
      proxy_pass         http://backend;
      proxy_set_header   Host $host;
      proxy_set_header   X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
      proxy_set_header   X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
      proxy_set_header   X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
    }

    # Static file uploads proxy
    location /uploads/ {
      proxy_pass http://backend/uploads/;
      proxy_set_header Host $host;
      expires 30d;
      add_header Cache-Control "public, no-transform";
    }

    # WebSocket for real-time notifications
    location /socket.io/ {
      proxy_pass http://backend/socket.io/;
      proxy_http_version 1.1;
      proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;
      proxy_set_header Connection "Upgrade";
      proxy_set_header Host $host;
      proxy_cache_bypass $http_upgrade;
    }

    # Swagger documentation
    location /api-docs {
      proxy_pass http://backend;
      proxy_set_header Host $host;
    }

    # Frontend SPA fallback
    location / {
      proxy_pass http://frontend;
      proxy_set_header Host $host;
      proxy_http_version 1.1;
      proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;
      proxy_set_header Connection "upgrade";
      try_files $uri $uri/ /index.html;
    }

    # Health check
    location /health {
      access_log off;
      return 200 "OK\n";
      add_header Content-Type text/plain;
    }
  }
}
</file>

<file path="project-rules/ARCHITECTURE.md">
# Architecture - LumicorePro Core

## Tech Stack
- **Frontend:** React 19 + Vite
- **Styling:** Tailwind CSS
- **Routing:** React Router DOM
- **HTTP Client:** Axios
- **Icons:** Lucide React
- **State Management:** React Context API

## Project Structure

```
lumicorepro-core/
├── src/
│   ├── components/       # Reusable UI components
│   │   ├── ui/           # Basic UI elements
│   │   ├── common/       # Shared components
│   │   ├── navigation/   # Navigation components
│   │   ├── forms/        # Form components
│   │   ├── ecommerce/    # E-commerce specific
│   │   ├── dashboard/    # Dashboard widgets
│   │   ├── ai/           # AI-related components
│   │   ├── business/     # Business logic UI
│   │   └── auth/         # Authentication UI
│   ├── icons/            # Icon exports by category
│   ├── assets/           # Images, fonts, logos
│   ├── pages/            # Page components
│   ├── layouts/          # Layout wrappers
│   ├── hooks/            # Custom React hooks
│   ├── services/         # API client & endpoints
│   ├── utils/            # Helper functions
│   ├── data/             # Static data & constants
│   ├── routes/           # React Router configuration
│   ├── styles/           # Global CSS & design system
│   └── context/          # React Context providers
├── project-rules/        # Development rules & standards
├── docs/                 # Documentation
├── backend/              # Backend API (future)
├── database/             # Database schema (future)
├── ai-agent/             # AI agent integration (future)
└── templates/            # Project templates (future)
```

## Architecture Principles

### Component Architecture
- **Pages** → high-level route components
- **Layouts** → wrap pages with common UI (navbar, footer)
- **Components** → reusable, self-contained UI pieces
- **Hooks** → custom logic extraction
- **Services** → API communication layer

### State Management
- **Local State:** `useState` for component-level state
- **Global State:** Context API for theme, auth, notifications
- **URL State:** React Router for navigation state

### API Layer
- Centralized Axios instance in `src/services/api.js`
- Request/response interceptors for auth tokens
- Environment-based API URL configuration
- Error handling with user-friendly messages

### Styling
- Tailwind CSS for utility-first styling
- Design system variables in `globals.css`
- Dark mode via CSS variables + class toggle
- Responsive breakpoints: sm, md, lg, xl, 2xl

## Data Flow
```
User Action → Component → Hook/Service → API → Response → State Update → Re-render
```

## Environment Variables
All prefixed with `VITE_` for Vite compatibility:
- `VITE_API_URL` - Backend API endpoint
- `VITE_ENV` - Development/Production
- `VITE_ENABLE_MOCK_API` - Toggle mock data
- `VITE_ENABLE_DARK_MODE` - Default theme
</file>

<file path="project-rules/COMPONENT_STANDARDS.md">
# Component Standards — LumicorePro Core

## Rules (simple & professional)

1. **One component per file** under the right category (`ui/`, `forms/`, `templates/…`).
2. **Tailwind first** — CSS modules only for rare complex cases.
3. **Design tokens** — use `primary`, `muted`, `border`, never hardcode brand colors.
4. **Props** — clear defaults: `variant`, `size`, `disabled`, `className`, event handlers.
5. **States** — default, hover, active, disabled, loading, focus, error where relevant.
6. **a11y** — `aria-*`, keyboard support, visible focus rings.
7. **Motion** — `transition-all duration-200`, respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.
8. **Docs** — short JSDoc with usage example on public components.

## Variants

`primary` · `secondary` · `success` · `danger` · `warning` · `info` · `outline` · `ghost`

## Sizes

`xs` · `sm` · `md` (default) · `lg` · `xl`
</file>

<file path="project-rules/MASTER_PROMPT.md">
# LumicorePro Core — Complete System Master Prompt

**Version:** 1.0  
**Status:** Production-ready blueprint  
**Scope:** Frontend (React + Vite) · Backend (Node + Express) · Database (MySQL) · AI

---

## System architecture

```
End User → React Frontend → Axios API Gateway → Express Backend → MySQL
                              ↘ Stripe / AI providers / Email / Uploads
```

---

## Frontend (`src/`)

| Area | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `components/ui` | Primitives (Button, Card, Modal, …) |
| `components/*` | Domain UI (dashboard, ecommerce, ai, business, forms, auth) |
| `templates/` | 20 production page templates |
| `pages/` | App routes (Home, Templates hub, Auth) |
| `layouts/` | Main / Auth / Dashboard shells |
| `hooks/` | useApi, useForm, useAuth, useCart, useReveal, … |
| `context/` | App, Auth, Cart, Theme |
| `services/` | api, auth, product, order, ai |
| `styles/` | tokens, animations |
| `config/` | app + theme config |

**Rules:** Tailwind-first · design tokens · a11y · motion 150–300ms · Lucide icons **with visible labels** (icon + name side by side).

---

## Backend (`backend/`)

```
backend/src/
  config/     database, env, cors, jwt
  routes/     auth, users, products, orders, cart, payments, ai, admin
  controllers/
  services/
  models/
  middleware/ auth, error, validation, rateLimit
  validators/
  utils/
  server.js
```

Standard response:

```json
{ "success": true, "status": 200, "message": "...", "data": {}, "timestamp": "..." }
```

---

## Database (MySQL)

Core domains:

1. **Auth** — users, sessions, password_resets  
2. **Catalog** — categories, products, product_images, product_variants, reviews  
3. **Commerce** — carts, cart_items, orders, order_items, payments  
4. **AI** — conversations, messages, ai_usage  
5. **SaaS** — plans, subscriptions, invoices  
6. **Admin** — audit_logs, settings  

SQL lives in `database/schema.sql`.

---

## API surface (summary)

- `POST/GET /api/auth/*` — register, login, logout, refresh, me, password reset  
- `GET/PUT /api/users/:id` — profile, avatar, password  
- `GET/POST /api/products` — list, detail, search, reviews (admin CRUD)  
- `GET/POST /api/cart` — items, coupon  
- `GET/POST /api/orders` — create, cancel, invoice, track  
- `POST /api/payments/stripe/*` — intent, confirm, webhook  
- `POST/GET /api/ai/*` — chat, conversations, generate, usage, models  
- `GET/PUT /api/admin/*` — users, stats, logs, settings  

Full endpoint list: see `docs/API.md` (when expanded) and `backend/src/routes/`.

---

## Security

- Access JWT ~15m · Refresh ~7d (httpOnly cookie preferred)  
- bcrypt (12 rounds) · parameterized SQL · CORS whitelist · rate limits · HTTPS in prod  

---

## Phases

| Phase | Focus | Status in repo |
|-------|--------|----------------|
| 1 | Vite + React foundation | Done |
| 2 | Config, hooks, standards | Done |
| 3 | Design system + motion | Done |
| 4 | 20 templates | Done |
| 5+ | Backend + DB + AI agent | Scaffolded / next |

---

## Success criteria

- Reusable UI + 20 templates  
- Auth + commerce + AI flows  
- MySQL schema + Express API scaffold  
- Professional UX: **every icon paired with a clear label**  
- Deployable frontend; backend ready to flesh out  

---

## Commands

```bash
# Frontend
npm run dev

# Backend (from backend/)
npm install && npm run dev
```

Open `/templates` for the gallery.
</file>

<file path="project-rules/PROJECT_RULES.md">
# Project Rules - LumicorePro Core

## Code Style
- Use functional components with hooks
- Use JSX syntax
- Follow ESLint + Prettier configuration
- 2-space indentation
- Single quotes for strings
- Semicolons required
- Max line length: 100 characters

## Naming Conventions
- Components: PascalCase (`MainLayout.jsx`)
- Utilities: camelCase (`helpers.js`)
- Hooks: camelCase with `use` prefix (`useWindowSize.js`)
- Constants: UPPER_SNAKE_CASE
- Files: match component name (PascalCase for components, camelCase for utilities)

## File Organization
- One component per file
- Export default for main components
- Named exports for utilities
- Keep files under 300 lines

## React Patterns
- Use React Router for navigation
- Use Context API for global state
- Use Axios for API calls
- Implement error boundaries
- Use `useEffect` cleanup for subscriptions

## Tailwind CSS
- Use Tailwind utility classes
- Custom styles in `globals.css`
- Responsive design first
- Dark mode support required

## Git Workflow
- Feature branches for new work
- Commit messages: "Type: description" (e.g., "feat: add home page")
- Keep commits small and focused
- Always pull before pushing

## Testing
- Write tests for utilities
- Test critical user flows
- Aim for 80%+ coverage

## Security
- Never commit `.env` files
- Validate all user input
- Use environment variables for secrets
- Sanitize API responses
</file>

